WEBVTT

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.520
Don’t let it escape.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.600
Take us lower!

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.290
Ma’am!

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.820
Huh? Nightmares?

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.990
Yes.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.620
There have been reports
from across Sinnoh...

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.320
...that entire cities have
had trouble sleeping.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.950
Is a Pokémon causing that?

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.640
That is likely.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.080
Nightmares in Sinnoh
brings to mind...

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.830
The Pitch-Black Pokémon,
Darkrai.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.780
It has the power to give
humans and Pokémon nightmares.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.210
Darkrai, huh?

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.200
I wouldn’t put it past that one...

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.370
You’ve <i>met</i> Darkrai, Satoshi?!

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:15.090
Yeah!

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:18.210
It’s strong in battle!
It’s an awesome Pokémon!

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.560
Right, Pikachu?

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.840
However, Darkrai usually stays
on New Moon Island,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.420
rarely ever leaving its home.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.410
Is there some reason for this?

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.030
Or is another Pokémon behind it...?

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.690
That’s what we’re
investigating, right?!

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.360
Oh! Quick as ever, Go!

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.990
Let’s go to Sinnoh!

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:37.740
Yeah!

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.990
We’re heading out!

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.020
Welcome back, Koharu!

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.660
Have a good trip!

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.200
They’re off on research?

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.540
Right.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.250
Welcome back, Koharu.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.920
You’re back early today.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.930
Yeah! Today was just the end-of-term ceremony
and summer vacation advice.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.170
Director!

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.020
The egg data check’s finished!

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:58.850
Got it.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:01:59.890
I’ll be right there.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:02.060
I’ll head home, then.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:03.760
Let’s go, Eevee!

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.310
Dad!

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.020
I’m really looking forward to
our family vacation!

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.250
Oh! For sure...

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.080
The family... vacation...

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.780
The vacation!

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.280
What?!

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.380
What do you mean
the vacation’s canceled?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.490
Well, uh...

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:04.180
The egg we’re looking after at the Institute
is on the verge of hatching...

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.010
I need to keep an eye on it.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.460
You need to keep an eye on it...?

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.600
Even though you have
Renji and Kikuna?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.190
Yeah... That’s right...

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.230
I’ve been looking after the egg thus far...

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.140
I want to be there
to care for it, or, well...

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:23.320
If I’m there to look it in the eyes,
I know it’ll understand how I feel.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.200
Oh, uh...

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.390
I apologize, Koharu!

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:33.170
And I just got an urgent
illustration job, too.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.040
Sorry!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.250
Aww...

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.200
But you promised we’d do this
for so long!

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.310
I was looking forward to our first
family vacation in ages.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.260
You want to go too,
right, Sota?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.340
I don’t really care.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.160
Huh?!

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.810
My friends invited me to summer camp,
so now I can go with them.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.920
H-How could you...

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.360
Oh, I know!

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.190
It just so happens that Satoshi and Go
had to go to Sinnoh to do research.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.580
Why don’t you go there
and meet up with them?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.280
What, help them with research
just because I have nothing better to do?

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.990
N-N-No...

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.220
You could enjoy yourself
while you’re there.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.320
And, of course, you can meet
lots of Pokémon there!

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.370
It’ll be fun!

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:14.620
Sometimes, you really seem to believe that
Pokémon make everything better, huh?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:15.080
Huh?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:19.510
I wanted to enjoy a vacation with
you, Mom, and Sota!

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.230
Oh, well, uh...

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.270
Forget it!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.260
Koharu...

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:31.010
If you won’t go,
Eevee and I will go on our <i>own</i> trip!

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.580
That’s fine, but Koharu...

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:35.310
Your suitcase.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.200
Don’t you think that’s a bit much?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.570
Here, take this.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:46.000
This should cover
most of the essentials.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.200
When I was your age,

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.310
I went traveling
with this backpack.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.540
You did?

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:53.750
Yeah!

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:56.170
Sorry about spoiling your vacation,

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.100
but this is a good chance to
go out and be free.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.080
Go and have some fun!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.630
Be free...

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:03.800
Yeah!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.630
Got it!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.080
If you have any problems,
or feel down,

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.550
please call us right away, okay?

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:11.000
Don’t treat me like a child.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:11.930
See you later.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.860
I’m actually here!

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:30.780
Sinnoh Region

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.850
This is kind of exciting...

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.680
Let’s have lots of fun, Eevee!

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.750
Eevee,
where would you like to go?

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.000
Sorry!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.040
Huh, a tourist?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:44.770
Huh?

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.210
Are you traveling alone?

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.460
Y-Yes.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.630
Oh, so you’re here to
take on our Gyms?

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.640
How about a battle, then?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.930
I-I don’t really...

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.060
Sorry!

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.160
Is there a tourist info center
anywhere...?

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:04.900
Joining us on the show today,

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.670
we have a lady who once claimed victory
in countless contests...

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:09.280
The legendary Pokémon Coordinator,

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.000
Ayako!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:16.200
Ayako, I hear a Pokémon Contest
is starting soon in Hakutai City?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:16.970
Yes.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.560
It’s shaping up to be
a very lively contest.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.750
I’m looking forward to
seeing the performances.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.310
A Pokémon Contest...

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:28.210
Eevee, are you interested?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.170
You are?

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.970
How about we
go watch that contest?

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.560
When’s the bus to Hakutai City...?

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:41.070
It’s an hour from now.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:42.760
That’s a bit of a wait, but...

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:45.720
What?

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:47.020
You want to walk there?!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.410
Sure, I guess!

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:55.160
We can enjoy all the scenery,
and maybe even see some rare Pokémon!

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:06.920
Mukkuru. Starling Pokémon.
Normal/Flying type.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.100
They flock in great numbers.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:12.170
Though small,
they flap their wings with great power.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:16.640
They’re so cute.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.860
S-Sorry!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.110
That was a shock...

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.920
W-Well... surprises like that
can still be fun, right?

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.400
You have to find the fun
in everything!

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:52.380
Maybe traveling is just trouble...

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.220
No.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.870
I can’t be thinking that.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.260
I am <i>not</i> feeling down!

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.520
Uh... Miss Junsa?

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:09.560
Oh, sorry...

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.650
You’re here to investigate
this city, right?

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:13.140
Yeah.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:16.140
We heard everyone was having nightmares
and couldn’t sleep.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:19.410
We think a Pokémon
might be causing it!

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.100
I see...

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.810
We keep getting woken up
by nightmares...

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:27.160
People are dozing off...
and causing accidents...

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.290
Or getting angry, and arguing...

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.530
Has anyone reported seeing
any suspicious Pokémon?

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:33.800
Like Darkrai!

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.680
I haven’t heard a thing.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.330
It happens while
people are asleep, anyway.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.020
Oh, but this phenomenon...

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.960
The next city over
had it last week,

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.460
and the village over there
before that.

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.310
It’s like it’s moving around
little by little.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.690
That’s <i>gotta</i> be a Pokémon!

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:51.710
Tracking its route might
help us learn something.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.570
Let’s start by asking around, Satoshi.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.660
I beg your pardon?!

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:59.320
You want us to catch
a runaway Cresselia in Sinnoh?!

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:00.330
Correct.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:02.200
Head out immediately.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.300
Why us?

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:07.080
That sounds like it’s <i>your</i> mistake.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.810
Absolutely nothing to do with us!

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.840
“Capture Darkrai and Cresselia.”

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.720
This mission was a direct order
from Sakaki.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.720
If you succeed,
it’ll improve your reputation.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.660
A direct order from Sakaki?!

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.200
Our reputation will skyrocket?!

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.720
Promotion guaranteed?!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.900
If you <i>absolutely refuse,</i>
I’ll find someone else.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.160
<i>We’ll do it!</i>

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.190
We’ll be right there!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.840
Then move quickly.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.610
If they succeed, then all is well.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.060
If they fail, it’ll be their fault.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:40.820
Whatever happens,
I won’t take the fallout.

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:43.850
We will pursue Darkrai!

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:44.870
Ma’am!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.670
Should we get going, then?

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.250
What’s that?

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.450
It’s so pretty!

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.860
What do you think, Eevee?

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.900
If we didn’t come here,
we wouldn’t have seen this beautiful lake.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.120
I’m glad we did!

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.140
It won’t light...

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:39.750
There’s lots of stuff in here,
but I don’t know what it’s all for...

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.820
J-Just hold on for now, Eevee.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:46.970
I’ll have dinner ready soon.

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:56.430
Yes! I finally got a light!

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:04.190
This looks good.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.630
You must be hungry.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:11.490
So, this is where
we’re sleeping tonight...

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.080
No dangerous Pokémon here,
at least.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.260
Hey, Pochama!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.350
A-Are you okay?

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:35.480
I’m fine, I’m fine...

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.320
Pocket Monsters!

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:49.740
You’re a huge help.

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:51.960
We were looking for
somewhere to camp...

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:54.540
...when we realized
we forgot to buy food,

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.270
and then this great smell
came wafting over!

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:00.130
I thought I was being attacked
by a wild Pokémon.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.660
Sorry about that...

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:04.090
My name’s Hikari.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.500
This is my partner, Pochama!

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.140
I’m Koharu.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.670
And this is Eevee.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.910
Nice to meet you, Eevee!

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.690
So, where are you headed?

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:20.020
I thought I’d go to Hakutai City.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:23.090
Oh, are you taking part
in the contest?!

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.780
I am, too!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.320
Oh, you are?

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.540
We’re just going to watch, though.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:29.160
Huh?

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.140
Why?

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:31.990
If you’re going anyway,
you should enter!

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:33.930
O-Oh, I couldn’t.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:35.210
I’ve never entered one before.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.810
It’s fine, it’s fine!

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:39.110
Everyone has to start
somewhere.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.330
Miss Hikari, have you...

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:41.460
Oh, just call me Hikari.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.970
Ah, sure.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:45.240
Hikari, have you entered
a contest before?

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:46.440
Of course!

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:50.000
I’ve been to pretty much
every contest venue in Sinnoh.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.670
Plus Hoenn’s, Isshu’s, and Johto’s.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:54.930
I’ve been all over.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.690
Wow! All by yourself?

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.850
Sometimes by myself,
sometimes with friends.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:03.280
When traveling around Sinnoh,
we were a group of three!

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.840
Huh.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:07.900
This is the first time
I’ve traveled alone.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.130
Hey, Koharu.

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.160
Why don’t we head to
Hakutai City together?

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.370
You sure?

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.820
Of course!

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.880
We’re back.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:27.880
We investigated the nightmares,
but couldn’t find out what was causing them.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.360
Huh?

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:31.530
Who cares about investigating?

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:35.150
Never mind that.
Did you catch any strong Pokémon?

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:37.320
Kikuna? Renji?

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.940
Is something wrong?

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.190
If you say “Is something wrong?”

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:50.290
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.360
To protect the world from devastation.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.450
To preserve world peace.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.370
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:03.340
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:04.830
Kikuna!

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:05.800
Renji!

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:09.400
The Team Sakuragi duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.720
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.440
T-Team Sakuragi?!

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:28.990
Sakuragi!

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:34.430
Launch an all-out assault
with all the Pokémon in Sakuragi Park!

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:37.470
Everything the world over
will belong to Sakuragi!

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:44.800
I just had this <i>really</i> bad dream...

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:45.980
Me, too!

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:48.670
Sarunori, you too?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:51.060
Does that mean...?

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:56.430
Darkrai!

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.060
Darkrai!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.680
So it really <i>was...</i>

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.190
Wh-What do I do?!

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:14.280
Good morning...

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.410
Ahh! Don’t look at me!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.700
What’s wrong?

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.970
See? Pochama’s very helpful!

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:34.720
Thank you, Pochama!

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:46.310
At this pace, we can sleep at
the Pokémon Center tonight.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:47.810
Yeah, that’s right.

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:52.000
A spring!

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.070
The water’s cool!

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.990
Hey, Koharu, come and feel this!

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.080
Sure!

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.710
Maybe the path on the right
would get us there quicker...

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:11.430
A Subomi! It’s so cute!

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.550
Look, Koharu!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.970
Oh, right.

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.550
Yes, it’s cute.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:25.270
Hikari!

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.270
It might be better if we hurry...

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:30.020
Oh! It’ll be fine, it’ll be fine!

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.530
It’ll be fine, it’ll be fine!

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.030
It’ll be fine, it’ll be fine!

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.530
It’ll be fine, it’ll be fine!

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.610
It is <i>not</i> going to be fine!

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:39.320
Oh, you can say that as
“It’ll be not fine!”

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:43.700
If we keep stopping,
the day’ll be over before we know it!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.540
If you’re traveling,
you should have some fun!

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:49.890
Look at the scenery,
not the guidebook.

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:51.250
I am having fun.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:54.800
I’m just saying
we should keep moving.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:56.650
Things will work out.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:58.590
Don’t be such a spoilsport, Koharu!

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.600
And I’d say you’re too thoughtless.

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.780
If I say it’ll be fine,
it’ll be fine!

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:04.030
It’ll be not fine!

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:05.420
It’ll be not-not fine!

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:06.770
It’ll be not-not-not fine!

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.850
It’ll be not-not-not-not fine!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:10.930
Okay...

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:12.360
Thank you.

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:15.730
Sounds like Darkrai
isn’t around here anymore.

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:19.240
What is it?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.600
Based on what the
nightmare victims described,

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.730
I tried calculating its route.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:30.130
But it just seems to be
wandering around this forest.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.330
You’re right...

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.380
Is something in there?

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:35.910
Should we go check?

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.170
Yeah!

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:41.680
If Cresselia fled Full Moon Island
and tried to hide,

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.990
it’d probably end up in this forest.

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:48.330
So we have to find one Cresselia
in this huge forest, meow?

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.640
We’ve got this!

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:54.350
We get promoted before that bowl-headed four-eyes,
then <i>we</i> can boss <i>her</i> around!

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:58.320
See? The sun did set.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:01.560
We could’ve made it to the village
if we kept walking.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:05.520
But we got to have fun instead,
and that’s what matters, right, Pochama?

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.830
You wanted to sleep in a nice bed,
didn’t you, Eevee?

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:20.970
A Saidon?!

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:29.420
Eevee! Tackle!

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:37.600
Eevee—

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.780
Koharu, leave it to me!

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:44.030
Water-type moves are effective on
the Ground/Rock-type Saidon.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.540
Pochama! Bubble Beam!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.210
Wow...

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:58.630
Pochama!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.530
Eevee...

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:11.420
I get it.

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:12.440
Bubble Beam!

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:15.900
Wha...?!

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:28.550
It fell asleep?

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:29.650
You did it...

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:33.180
Wow! How come your Eevee
can use Bubble Beam?!

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:34.090
Oh, uh...

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:36.710
Pochama was amazing
too, though!

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:48.260
What...?

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:58.230
If we find Darkrai,
we might end up having to battle it.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:20:59.740
Maybe.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.920
Let’s be careful not to fall asleep!

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.570
If only Cresselia was here...

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.240
Cresselia...

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:12.870
Oh, yeah. Cresselia’s crescent feathers have the power
to dispel Darkrai’s nightmares, don’t they?

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:14.260
Yeah.

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:15.180
Let’s go!

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:16.020
Yeah!

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.070
That’s...

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:35.690
Koharu and Hikari have found
a badly wounded Cresselia in the woods.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:38.770
All the while, Satoshi and Go
are pursuing Darkrai.

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:43.270
What fate lies in store
for the four of them?

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.580
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.780
Go!

00:23:11.930 --> 00:23:14.190
Who did this to Cresselia?

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:16.700
Could it be... Darkrai?!

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:18.320
Huh? Hikari!

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:19.540
Huh? Satoshi?!

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:20.960
Huh? Huh?!

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:23.170
Satoshi and Hikari,
you know each other?

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:30.830
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:33.850
Cresselia: A Midsummer Night’s Light!
